USE OF 'this' keyword

1. To differentiate between global variables and parameters with the same name
2. To call one constructor inside of other constructor
    -> Constructor calling should always be the first statement inside another constructor
    -> we cannot call a constructor inside of a method
3.  We can call non-static method inside of another non-static method of the same class using this keyword
      -> either using class name [if called method is static]
      -> either through object reference variable [non -static method]
      -> using this keyword [non-static method inside of other non static method of the same class]

4. Builder pattern

